  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l03_initialize_edge_statistics(legal_actions: list, prior_probs: list, num_actions: int = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Initialize Monte Carlo Tree Search edge statistics when expanding a newly visited state node, ensuring illegal actions receive zero probability and legal actions receive normalized prior probabilities from the policy network.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nInitialize Monte Carlo Tree Search edge statistics when expanding a newly visited state node, ensuring illegal actions receive zero probability and legal actions receive normalized prior probabilities from the policy network.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l03_initialize_edge_statistics(legal_actions: list, prior_probs: list, num_actions: int = None) -> dict:\n    if num_actions is None:\n        num_actions = len(prior_probs)\n    N = np.zeros(num_actions, dtype=float)\n    W = np.zeros(num_actions, dtype=float)\n    Q = np.zeros(num_actions, dtype=float)\n    P = np.zeros(num_actions, dtype=float)\n    raw_p = np.array(prior_probs, dtype=float)\n    mask = np.zeros(num_actions, dtype=bool)\n    for a in legal_actions:\n        if 0 <= a < num_actions:\n            mask[a] = True\n    legal_mass = np.sum(raw_p[mask])\n    if legal_mass > 0:\n        P[mask] = raw_p[mask] / legal_mass\n    elif len(legal_actions) > 0:\n        P[mask] = 1.0 / len(legal_actions)\n    return {'N': N.tolist(), 'W': W.tolist(), 'Q': Q.tolist(), 'P': np.round(P, 6).tolist()}\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
